    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • OMODA 4 Lands in Paris To Showcase Futuristic Styling, Looks Like a Discount Urus\nAll-New Toyota Land Cruiser EV Renderings Put the Electric CUV Right Next to the Off-Road SUV Boss\n6 photos\nPhoto: kelsonik / Instagram\nThe Japanese automaker is doing a lot of things lately: testing their next mid-engine coupe, recalling J250-generation Land Cruisers for a fuel leak fire risk, trying to convince the European Union that some hybrids are actually zero-emission models, or potentially fitting the next Corolla generation with ICE, hybrid, and full EV powertrains, among other things – like updating its American models to the 2027 model year standards.\nJust recently, though, Subaru did one interesting EV thing without the help of its all-electric model partner, Toyota. More precisely, they built a 510-hp electric wagon featuring dual motors, lighter hardware, plus an integrated control unit to show how its EV platform could evolve and reach the next generation of all-wheel drive models.\nSo, it’s no wonder that Toyota also has a new EV – though only across the parallel universes of vehicular CGI and courtesy of the members of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators. More precisely, Nikita Chuicko, the virtual artist better known as \" kelsonik \" on social media, thinks that now is the right CGI time to work on a new Toyota – the Land Cruiser EV.\nThe new model is being developed based on the Land Cruiser Se concept and could be introduced around 2027, though maybe not in America , where the latest iteration of the Highlander, now completely electric, has been recently postponed due to the grim prospects of the EV market in the United States.\nNevertheless, the rumor mill believes that development is ongoing for a launch next year, complete with a new unibody architecture that till clearly set it apart from both the current J250 and J300 Land Cruiser models. It will probably focus on family versatility and city driving, rather than the great outdoors. Many outlets expect it to feature a five- or seven-seat arrangement to clash with rivals like the Kia EV9, and while initial models will arrive with current battery packs, the Land Cruiser EV could also serve as Toyota’s debut model for high-performance solid-state battery options.\nAnyway, the pixel master doesn’t have much to say about the dual-motor all-wheel drive powertrain options – he’s more preoccupied with showcasing the all-new, first-ever Toyota Land Cruiser EV in his latest unofficial, hypothetical design project based on the newest spy photos. The design features a new styling ethos for the Land Cruiser, with slim LED headlights, a boxy side profile that’s wide and muscular but also more streamlined than the ICE and hybrid SUV siblings, plus a rear featuring a simple look underpinned by a new full-width LED taillight signature.\nLast but not least, perhaps to better understand the upcoming design changes, the CGI expert also drops the newly rendered Toyota Land Cruiser EV based on the latest spy shots alongside the round-headlight version of the current Toyota Land Cruiser (Prado). View this post on Instagram A post shared by CAR DESIGN | RENDERINGS (@kelsonik)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nToyota Land Cruiser EV Toyota Land Cruiser EV Land Cruiser J250 CGI EV crossover SUV rendering kelsonik\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Dodge Charger SRT Hellcat Races R35 Nissan GT-R, Someone Wins the Fight By Just One Mile Per Hour",
